    [Refactor][Patch] Use upstream GLM-5-Next config support (#18930)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    vLLM v0.31.0 and the verified main pin
    (`c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b`) already register
    `glm5_next`, `glm5_next_text`, and `glm5_next_vision`, and recognize the
    GLM-5-Next text model types for MLA. The upstream config classes have
    the same implementation as the downstream classes after normalizing
    formatting and the `PreTrainedConfig` spelling.
    
    Remove `patch_glm5next_config.py`, its platform import, its patch
    documentation, and the duplicate local config module. Import the
    upstream config classes in the Ascend model, attention, KDA, and MTP
    unit test so the test constructs the same upstream `Glm5NextTextConfig`
    used for model loading. The Ascend model registrations remain in place.
    
    Upstream support: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53906
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Config registration and MLA detection use the equivalent upstream
    implementations in the supported vLLM versions.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci`: passed using ARM64 Gitleaks 8.30.1 and ShellCheck
    0.10.0. The default Gitleaks download was incompatible with ARM64; the
    installed ShellCheck failed to create its runtime ticker thread.
    - `git diff --check`: passed.
    - `python -m compileall -q vllm_ascend/patch/__init__.py
    vllm_ascend/patch/platform/__init__.py vllm_ascend/models/glm5next
    tests/ut/models/test_glm5_next_mtp.py`: passed.
    - Focused CPU source probes against both vLLM v0.31.0 and the verified
    main pin: confirmed all three registry entries and config-class AST
    equivalence; instantiated config classes using the existing
    `glm53flash_assets` text, nested multimodal, flat legacy, and vision
    configurations; compared serialized configs, layer layouts, and MoE
    detection. Upstream MLA detection also passed for both text model types
    with and without `kv_lora_rank`. These probes executed the extracted
    config classes and MLA method without the Ascend patch or a full vLLM
    runtime.
    - Verified no remaining `patch_glm5next_config` references in source or
    tests.
    
    The updated existing MTP unit tests passed against both supported vLLM
    references (4 passed on each), including the test that directly
    constructs the upstream text config and checks its conversion to
    `Glm5NextMTPModel`:
    
    ```bash
    TORCH_DEVICE_BACKEND_AUTOLOAD=0 PYTHONPATH=/path/to/pinned-vllm:$PWD python -m pytest -q tests/ut/models/test_glm5_next_mtp.py
    ```
    
    These runs used the repository's CPU UT mocks, with inaccessible
    directories removed from `PATH` so the NPU availability check followed
    its CPU fallback. No new tests were added because the existing MTP test
    now exercises the upstream class directly. NPU execution remains
    unverified locally; the existing integration smoke for CI or hardware
    is:
    
    ```bash
    pytest -q tests/e2e/pull_request/four_card/test_glm5_3_flash.py
    ```
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
